SCIENTIFIC USE RESTRICTION

The MIT licence grants you permission to use, copy, modify and redistribute this
software. It does NOT grant permission to misrepresent what it does, and the
following is a binding representation rather than a request:

This software implements classical computer-vision image analysis. It loads no
neural network, measures no subjective experience, and reproduces no biological
altered state. The word "perception" throughout the codebase and documentation is
a metaphor for output-structure analysis.

If you use this software, you may not present its output as evidence about
consciousness, subjective experience, psychedelic phenomenology, or neural-network
internal states. It cannot support such a claim, and doing so misrepresents both
the software and any record of work using it.

The perception divergence score has no validated interpretation scale. No
threshold in this software has been empirically established as the boundary
between "no effect" and "an effect".
